// First authored player spell using RapidRanged (prior usage is all
// NPC/weapon abilities -- assets/common/abilities/bow/fusillade.ron,
// staff/pyroclasm.ron -- never a spell RON before this one).
//
// Real behavior confirmed by reading common/src/states/rapid_ranged.rs:
// every projectile fires along the SAME data.inputs.look_dir each shot
// (there is no per-projectile spread/homing field on RapidRanged, unlike
// BasicRanged's projectile_spread). `options.fire_all: true` +
// `max_projectiles: Some(2)` fires both beams back-to-back in one cast.
// The flavor text ("chosen foes") implies independently-aimed beams that
// can each hit a different creature; this engine's RapidRanged cannot
// express that -- both beams travel the same line, so in practice they
// will usually land on the same first target unless the caster's aim
// visibly moves between the two shoot ticks. Documented drop, not
// silently invented: no per-projectile independent-aim primitive exists.
//
// Damage split across 2 independent-rolling beams so total cantrip output
// (8+8=16) lands in the same band as this wave's single-shot cantrips
// (chill_touch 14, poison_spray 16 -- see
// assets/common/abilities/spells/hollow/). damage_kind: Force is exactly
// representable here (RapidRanged's `projectile.attack.damage_kind` is
// fully RON-configurable, unlike BasicMelee/Explosion/GroundAoe/BasicBeam,
// which all hardcode their DamageKind in Rust -- see this batch's other
// RONs for where that constraint forced a drift note).
RapidRanged(
    energy_cost: 0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    shoot_duration: 0.05,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    options: (
        max_projectiles: Some(2),
        fire_all: true,
    ),
    projectile: (
        kind: Simple,
        attack: Some((
            damage: 8,
            damage_kind: Force,
        )),
    ),
    projectile_body: Object(BoltFire),
    projectile_speed: 70.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
